  "target_contract": [
    "Unique owner and actual shared raw payload per logic frame; demand is union of enabled consumers, inflight tasks and display views.",
    "Static assets and resource metadata use explicit change/generation caching; dynamic world facts use logic-frame acquisition; small UI/view/input facts use an independent fast path.",
    "Original native member tables preserve order, completeness and failures; overlapping raw byte ranges deduplicate across collectors.",
    "Pure capture performs no native queries, events or game writes; independent live frame/world guards validate acquisition before seal.",
    "Sealed FrameRead has no ProcessReader or live fallback; uncovered new world demand waits for a subsequent logic frame.",
    "Native queries and execution use explicit LiveRead; identity, permission, manual token, lease, roster proof and immediate retirement requirements remain.",
    "Geometry-independent world/cells feed native Radar, Tactical overview, main and watch projection without recovering omitted objects from filtered legacy Frames.",
    "RawCombat and GameView combat decoder semantics remain separate; fresh selector and existing 30-frame derived metadata cache are not conflated.",
    "Cross-process Host/Runtime sharing requires versioned payload/coverage/lifetime, not only identical frame stamps.",
    "Source operation counts, physical reads, capture frequency, drawing rate and game FPS are different metrics."
  ],
